---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Note from "../../components/Note.astro";
const title = "retentive memory — the dysfunctional executives";
---
<BaseLayout {title}>
  <article class="container">
    <h1>retentive memory</h1>
    <p>retentive memory is the ability to hold and recall information. adhd brains often have strong retentive memory for topics of hyperfocus and weak memory for mundane stuff. rather than fighting this, work with it: externalize routine info (write it down, automate it) and leverage your strong memory for deep learning when something grabs you.</p>

    <ul>
      <li>use spaced repetition for things you want to retain (anki, flashcards)</li>
      <li>teach others; explaining cements memory</li>
      <li>connect new info to existing knowledge (it sticks better)</li>
      <li>write by hand when learning; typing is faster but memory is weaker</li>
      <li>accept your memory's shape: some people excel at faces, others at conversations, others at facts. play to yours.</li>
    </ul>

    <Note variant="try">track what sticks easily for you. notice patterns. build on your natural retention strengths.</Note>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
